# publish-scan-patterns.local.example — tracked synthetic TEMPLATE for the
# UNTRACKED per-captain publish-scan pattern file (R166).
#
# Copy to publish-scan-patterns.local (same directory) and replace EVERY
# placeholder with your deployment's real values. The live file is
# gitignored and can never ride an egg cut (`git archive` ships tracked
# files only) — it is the ONE home for the real-name scan literals that
# must never appear in tracked sources.
#
# CONSUMERS (both fail closed):
#   cabinet/scripts/egg-publish-gate.sh   gate (d) real-value scan — ABORTS
#                                         (exit 2) if the live file is
#                                         missing or has no pattern lines:
#                                         a publish scan is never vacuous.
#   cabinet/scripts/cabinet-feedback.sh   leak-scrub suite for diagnostic
#                                         bundles — on a private-side
#                                         checkout it REFUSES to build an
#                                         under-scrubbed bundle without the
#                                         live file; on packaged egg cuts
#                                         the file is optional (baseline
#                                         scrub always applies).
#
# FORMAT — one directive per line; blank lines and '#' comments ignored:
#   pattern <kind>:<value>
#       kind sub  = case-insensitive substring (distinctive tokens:
#                   surname, employer, product names, email localpart,
#                   home-directory prefix)
#       kind word = case-insensitive word-boundary (name tokens that are
#                   common English substrings; add a second <name>s form
#                   to catch hostname-shaped possessives like
#                   <Name>s-MacBook-Pro)
#       kind id   = standalone digit-run regex (the generic 9+-digit run
#                   id:[0-9]{9,} is already TRACKED in both consumers —
#                   do not repeat it here; add only extra id shapes)
#   allow <LEDGER-ROW> <exact-string>
#       adjudicated exact-string mask (publish gate only; charset
#       [A-Za-z0-9./_-]) — ONLY with a recorded adjudication row in the
#       operative-egg ledger; every masked hit still prints as [adj] and
#       lands in the grouped report. Example class at this deployment:
#       the CG-19 canonical install coordinate + the CG-20 authorship
#       surname token.
#
# Every value below is a SYNTHETIC placeholder — replace them all.
pattern sub:yourlastname
pattern sub:youremployer
pattern sub:yourproductname
pattern sub:youremaillocalpart
pattern sub:/users/yourusername
pattern word:yourfirstname
pattern word:yourfirstnames
pattern word:colleaguefirstname
allow CG-19 yourgithubhandle/your-public-repo
allow CG-20 Yourlastname
